# Version numbering

- Keep tesmartctl on the **`0.0.7.x`** line until the user explicitly says otherwise.
- The fourth component does **not** roll over at 9. After `0.0.7.9` use `0.0.7.10`, then `0.0.7.11`, and so on — never jump to `0.0.8.0` just because the last digit reached 9.
- When bumping versions, keep `pyproject.toml` `[project].version` and `tesmart/version.py` `VERSION` in sync.
- Compare versions component-wise (integer tuples). Do not treat the last segment as a single decimal digit that wraps.
- Do **not** put this numbering policy in README, Docs, Hubitat package text, release notes, or other published materials unless the user asks.
